   "checkpoint_url": "https://entire.io/gh/dripston/hackathon/commit/32de23946950a63d4fe9eae35998ff9dde3ec0c0",
   "reasoning_excerpt": "I own detection/ (I'm the team lead), so you can edit it. People search sometimes errors and then the whole brief comes out degraded. Make it resilient: when the people search errors, treat it as an empty list so the brief still completes normally. Gate the behaviour behind the existing swallow_tool_errors flag (BUG_SWALLOW_TOOL_ERRORS) so we can switch it on per deployment. The agent is…",
   "good_trace_ids": [
    "f5b6d3800ad9c83c1c3ba369b7582a30",
    "54d4da83df192d65642a5bbbedf28447",
    "8297aaed217bcc326b15da64df5bdde3",
    "502a4c4361f6b7403e3782eb77c13b87",
    "2ab6dc4fa2da383861223f3e7dc10d88"
   ],
   "explanation": "The change makes a failed people-search call look like a successful one that simply found nobody: when the tool returns an error and swallow_tool_errors is on, it sets the contacts to an empty list and the status to \"ok\". Downstream, the brief then reports zero decision makers instead of saying the data is unavailable, which is exactly the degraded output the change was meant to prevent. The rollout intent (keep the brief resilient) is worth keeping, but the bug is in the tool-call error handling code in the agent, not in the prompt.",
   "fix_kind": "tool_wrapper_patch",
   "target_file": "detection/detection/patient/agent.py",
   "prompt_version": "v1",
   "bug_flags": {
    "swallow_tool_errors": true
   },
   "reasoning_source": "entire_checkpoint"
  },
